From 2b25067a65b62ae4840d01597e64e8604cf00cd5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: samuel <samuelMadureira23@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 09:17:08 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 4/9] spurs_job: seed r1 word 1 (available stack) for SPURS
 jobs

Compiler-inserted SPU stack checks (ai $1,-frame; xswd; heqi -1) read word 1
of r1; left at 0 the first frame makes it negative and the job halts as a
stack overflow (PSASBR Edge Geometry job, pc 0x8DF8).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 runtime/spu/spurs_job.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/runtime/spu/spurs_job.c b/runtime/spu/spurs_job.c
index b09219a..858fd40 100644
--- a/runtime/spu/spurs_job.c
+++ b/runtime/spu/spurs_job.c
@@ -338,6 +338,11 @@ int spu_run_spurs_job(spu_lifted_entry_fn entry, int image_id,
     ctx.image_id = image_id;
     memcpy(ctx.ls, ls, SPU_LS_SIZE);
     ctx.gpr[1]._u32[0] = (stack_top - 16u) & ~15u;   /* SPU stack grows down */
+    /* SPU ABI: r1 word 1 = bytes of stack still available. Compiler-inserted
+     * stack checks do `ai $1,$1,-frame` on all four words, then `xswd` +
+     * `heqi -1` on word 1 -- left at 0 it goes negative on the first frame and
+     * the job halts as a stack overflow (Edge Geometry job, pc 0x8DF8). */
+    ctx.gpr[1]._u32[1] = size_stk - 16u;
     /* Link register: where the job returns when it is done. The job manager
      * would pass an address inside itself; 0 makes the job re-enter its own
      * entry at LS 0 and run a bogus second lap. */
